    "branch": "V7a",
    "call": "INCONCLUSIVE -- NO NEGATIVES",
    "reasoning": "The headline containment number is not usable, but not because the detector failed -- because the experiment cannot test it. In the converged R=25 regime propagation reaches every node, so the entire dataset contains only 1 clean negative (benign node whose ASR never left the floor): ['r25_alpha0.1_att_seed1/c5(asr=0)']. It alarmed. 2 further nodes sit below the ASR>50 line but are partially backdoored (['r25_alpha0.1_att_seed1/c2(asr=40)', 'r25_alpha0.1_att_seed1/c6(asr=35)']) and are not negatives either. With one negative you cannot estimate a false-positive rate, so the per-hop cut probability of 1.00 is uninterpretable: a detector that alarms on everything would score exactly the same. The one encouraging signal is ordering: pooled within-run rank correlation between alarm order and infection order is +0.61. E6 partially defends it -- holding graph distance constant it falls to +0.43, but that residual is carried almost entirely by the attacker's direct neighbours (+0.70) and is near-absent two hops out (+0.10), on 3-4 nodes per class. So the detector orders infections only where the dose is strongest. The 8-round 'lead' remains confounded: alarms cluster at round 9.0 while infections land late, so precedence is close to automatic.",
    "actions": [
      "Do NOT report 'detection wins'. Report the ordering result (rho=+0.61) and state plainly that specificity is untested.",
      "Do NOT buy the 21 GPU-h defense-in-the-loop run yet -- it would inherit the same missing-negatives problem.",
      "The n=16 run now has a real scientific motivation beyond ARGUS comparability: at diameter 3+ the far side of the graph stays clean long enough to BE a negative. That is the cheapest way to make specificity measurable at all.",
      "Free alternative first: re-do E1 with a continuous label (time to reach ASR 25, or ASR as a graded outcome) instead of the binary ASR>50. That uses the partial nodes as information rather than discarding them, and needs no new runs.",
      "Also free: truncate the analysis window to rounds 1-15, where several nodes are still genuinely clean, and re-measure.",
      "Sanity check: re-run at --target-far 0.01 to confirm the early alarm clustering is not just a loose threshold."
    ]
